A '''glow lichen''' is a non-solid, light-emitting [[block]]. It can generate, or be placed, on any side of a solid block. It primarily generates on the side of blocks in caves.

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Glow lichen can be destroyed with anything, most efficiently with an [[axe]]. However, using [[shears]] is the only way to obtain glow lichen. [[Enchanting]] shears with [[Efficiency]] II allows for instant mining.
{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Glow Lichen|Axe|drop=0|shears=1|sword=0}}

=== Natural generation ===
{{main|Glow lichen (feature)}}

Glow lichen generates naturally in the interior of caves (at any height) on the surface of [[stone]], [[sulfur]], [[cinnabar]], [[andesite]], [[diorite]], [[granite]], [[calcite]], [[tuff]], [[deepslate]], any [[ore]], and [[dripstone block]]s that are exposed to [[air]] or [[water]] sources. As well as within or upon generated structures, or sometimes even exposed to some surface light.  It can be found underwater, but cannot generate in a [[deep dark]] biome.

{{block distribution}}

=== Post-generation ===
{{relevant tutorial|Glow Lichen farming}}
{{Control|Using}} [[bone meal]] causes glow lichen to spread to a random adjacent block if possible; otherwise, the bone meal is not consumed. By fertilizing one lichen with bone meal, it is possible to cover the sides and the top of an adjacent block, but not the back. Otherwise, glow lichen does not spread naturally.

== Usage ==
=== Light ===
Glow lichen emits a [[light]] level of 7. With the "Render Dragon Features for Creators" [[experiment]], glow lichen has a [[light color]] of {{color|#b7f1bc}}.

=== Placement ===
Multiple glow lichens can be placed in the area of one solid block, such as covering three sides of a corner. When such glow lichens are mined, all glow lichens occupying the same block are also mined. Mining with [[shears]] causes all glow lichens in the block to drop.

Glow lichens cannot be broken by flowing [[water]] or [[lava]],<ref>{{bug|MC-212116||Flowing water cannot break glow lichen|WAI}}</ref><ref>{{bug|MCPE-133803||Glow Lichen interrupts water flow|WAI}}</ref> similar to [[sign]]s. Therefore, they may be used to control the flow of water, but not lava, as glow lichens are flammable.

=== Composting ===
Placing a glow lichen into a [[composter]] has a 50% chance of raising the compost level by 1.

